diff --git a/ambiguities/2025.yaml b/ambiguities/2025.yaml
index c99d012..02dd23e 100644
--- a/ambiguities/2025.yaml
+++ b/ambiguities/2025.yaml
@@ -2673,3 +2673,18 @@ register:
           qualified LTC services provided for the insured for LTC periods in 2025"'
       status: Planning lane plan-med-income (BUG-0873, owner decision 3), drafted in lane v2-income, 2026-11-16; for the
         owner.
+    - id: amb.2025.f8853c_line25_floor
+      text_at_issue: 'Form 8853 (2025), Section C, line 25: "Per diem limitation. Subtract line 24 from line 23" (no instruction for a
+        result below zero), and line 26: "Taxable payments. Subtract line 25 from line 20. If zero or less, enter -0-".
+        When the reimbursements on line 24 are more than line 23, the printed subtraction on line 25 is negative.'
+      readings:
+      - Line 25 is the printed subtraction and may be negative, so line 26 can be more than the payments on line 20.
+      - Line 25 is floored at zero (a limitation of zero), so the taxable payments on line 26 are never more than line 20.
+      chosen: The second (f8853c.line25 is subtract_floor0).
+      reason: Line 25 is named a limitation on the payments excluded; a negative limitation would tax, through line 26, more
+        than the per diem payments received on lines 17 to 20, and no text of the form or i8853 says reimbursements are
+        taxed there. The two readings differ only when line 24 is more than line 23 (rare).
+      cite:
+        doc: f8853
+        locator: Form 8853 (2025), line 25, "Per diem limitation. Subtract line 24 from line 23"
+      status: Planning lane lows-inc (BUG-0917), drafted 2026-11-16; for the owner.
